        ],
        "title": "RegisterRequest",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "RegisterResponse": {
        "description": "🔒 Carries no tokens and no identifiers.\n\nVerification precedes access (FR-M0-002), and the body is byte-identical\nwhether or not the address was already registered (NFR-043) — returning a\n`tenant_id` on the success path alone would restore the oracle the flat\nresponse exists to remove.",
        "properties": {
          "email_verification_required": {
            "const": true,
            "default": true,
            "title": "Email Verification Required",
            "type": "boolean"
          }
        },
        "title": "RegisterResponse",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "SexType": {
        "description": "Biological sex, for requirement estimation — DB §5.1.\n\n⚠️ 🟡 **PROPOSED — the value set is not specified in any approved document.**\nDB §5.1 names the column and the type and stops there. These values are my\nproposal and need confirmation.\n\n🔒 The column exists for one purpose: BMR equations (Mifflin-St Jeor,\nHarris-Benedict) take a male/female term. It is **nullable**, and ``OTHER``\nis a real answer rather than a gap — but neither NULL nor ``OTHER`` yields a\ndefined equation, so both must fall through to the practitioner entering a\nrequirement directly. Silently substituting one for the other would put a\nwrong number on a clinical plan, which is the failure this note exists to\nprevent.",
        "enum": [
          "male",
          "female",
          "other"
        ],
        "title": "SexType",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "TokenResponse": {
        "description": "What a client needs to make an authenticated request and to renew.\n\n🔒 No user object. The client fetches its own profile from a dedicated\nendpoint; embedding one here would put a name and email in every token\nrefresh and in whatever logs the response passes through.",
        "properties": {
          "access_token": {
            "title": "Access Token",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "expires_in": {
            "title": "Expires In",
            "type": "integer"
          },
          "refresh_token": {
            "title": "Refresh Token",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "token_type": {
            "const": "Bearer",
            "default": "Bearer",
            "title": "Token Type",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "access_token",
          "refresh_token",
          "expires_in"
        ],
        "title": "TokenResponse",
        "type": "object"
      },
